@media (prefers-reduced-motion: no-preference){#bench-art .fusedbar{transition:transform .3s ease}}</style></head><body><main class="lab"><header><p class="kicker">Information science (maths of ranking), Form 4 to 5</p><h1>Reciprocal rank fusion: merging two rankings</h1><p class="try"><strong>Try this:</strong> Drag the two round handles along their tracks to change where one document ranks in each list.</p></header><div class="top"><section class="card idea"><h2>Key idea</h2><p>Your question is about computing, not science, so this lab uses the closest thing a student can explore: a simple scoring formula. Each list gives a document a score of 1 divided by (k + rank), and the fused score is the sum of the two. A small rank number (near the front) gives a big score. Here k = 10 so the differences are easy to see; real systems often use k = 60.</p><p>fused score = 1/(k + keyword rank) + 1/(k + vector rank)</p></section><section class="card predict"><h2>Predict first</h2><p>Document A is rank 1 in the keyword list but rank 20 in the vector list. Document B is rank 5 in both lists. Which document gets the higher fused score?</p><ul><li>Document A, because rank 1 is the best possible</li><li>Document B, because it is good in both lists</li><li>They get exactly the same score</li></ul><details><summary>Check your prediction</summary><p>set keyword rank 1 and vector rank 20 and note the fused score, then set both ranks to 5 and compare.</p></details></section></div><section class="card steps"><h2>Steps</h2><ol><li>Drag the keyword handle from rank 1 to rank 20 while the vector rank stays the same. Watch the keyword score and the fused bar shrink.</li><li>Set both handles to rank 1, then move only the vector handle to rank 20. Watch how much of the fused score is lost.</li><li>Find two different pairs of ranks that give nearly the same fused score. Watch the bar length to compare them.</li></ol></section><section class="benchrow" aria-label="The lab bench"><div class="bench"><svg id="bench-art" viewBox="0 0 400 260" role="img" aria-label="Keyword rank 1 and vector rank 1 give a fused score of 181.8 thousandths">
<text x="60" y="38">Keyword rank</text>
